# one-context-vyos

This package adapts the OpenNebula Linux contextualization service to VyOS.
It reads the standard `CONTEXT` disk and supports the existing OpenNebula
context variables, including `ETH<N>_*`, `ONEGATE_ENDPOINT`, `ONEGATE_TOKEN`,
SSH keys, passwords, start scripts, and reconfiguration.

The `netcfg-vyos` backend configures these values through the native VyOS CLI:

- IPv4 and IPv6 interface addresses and aliases
- DHCP, DHCPv6, and IPv6 SLAAC
- Interface MTU
- IPv4 and IPv6 default and static routes
- A link-local route to the OneGate proxy
- System DNS servers and search domains
- `SET_HOSTNAME`

Every transaction is committed and saved to `/config/config.boot`. The exact
commands owned by contextualization are stored in
`/config/one-context/network.commands`. During reconfiguration, the previous
owned commands are deleted before the new desired commands are applied. Other
VyOS configuration remains untouched.

The package provides and conflicts with `one-context`; install it instead of
the generic Debian package:

```sh
sudo dpkg -i one-context-vyos_7.4.0-0.deb
```

The generated environment for appliance services is available at
`/run/one-context/one_env`. `TOKENTXT` contains the token itself, not a path.
